Feel the need... The need for speed.

2
00:09:02,068 --> 00:09:08,068
Top Gun: Maverick is a action, drama film directed by Joseph Kosinski.

3
00:13:33,103 --> 00:13:39,103
After more than thirty years of service as one of the Navy’s top aviators, and dodging the advancement in rank that would ground him, Pete “Maverick”
Mitchell finds himself training a detachment of TOP GUN graduates for a specialized mission the likes of which no living pilot has ever seen.

4
00:18:04,137 --> 00:18:10,137
Capt. Pete 'Maverick' Mitchell, played by Tom Cruise.

5
00:22:35,172 --> 00:22:41,172
Adm. Tom 'Iceman' Kazansky, played by Val Kilmer.

6
00:27:06,206 --> 00:27:12,206
Lt. Bradley 'Rooster' Bradshaw, played by Miles Teller.

7
00:31:37,241 --> 00:31:43,241
Penny Benjamin, played by Jennifer Connelly.

8
00:36:08,275 --> 00:36:14,275
Wo-1. Bernie 'Hondo' Coleman, played by Bashir Salahuddin.

9
00:40:39,310 --> 00:40:45,310
Adm. Beau 'Cyclone' Simpson, played by Jon Hamm.

10
00:45:10,344 --> 00:45:16,344
Top Gun: Maverick is a 2022 American action drama film directed by Joseph Kosinski and written by Ehren Kruger,
Eric Warren Singer, and Christopher McQuarrie, from a story by Peter Craig and Justin Marks.

11
00:49:41,379 --> 00:49:47,379
In this sequel to the 1986 film Top Gun, Tom Cruise reprises his
starring role as the naval aviator Pete "Maverick" Mitchell.

12
00:54:12,413 --> 00:54:18,413
The ensemble cast also features Miles Teller, Jennifer Connelly, Jon Hamm, Glen Powell, Monica
Barbaro, Lewis Pullman, Ed Harris, and Val Kilmer (in his final film role).

13
00:58:43,448 --> 00:58:49,448
The story involves Maverick confronting his past while training a group of younger Top Gun
graduates, including the son of his deceased best friend, for a dangerous mission.

14
01:03:14,482 --> 01:03:20,482
Development of a Top Gun sequel was announced in 2010 by Paramount Pictures.

15
01:07:45,517 --> 01:07:51,517
Cruise, along with co-producer Jerry Bruckheimer and
director Tony Scott, were asked to return.

16
01:12:16,551 --> 01:12:22,551
Craig wrote a draft of the screenplay in 2012, but the
project stalled when Scott died later that year.

17
01:16:47,586 --> 01:16:53,586
Top Gun: Maverick was later dedicated to Scott's memory.

18
01:21:18,620 --> 01:21:24,620
Production resumed in 2017, after Kosinski was hired to direct.

19
01:25:49,655 --> 01:25:55,655
Principal photography, which involved the use of IMAX-certified 6K full-frame cameras, took
place from May 2018 to April 2019 in California, Washington, and Maryland.

20
01:30:20,689 --> 01:30:26,689
The film's complex action sequences—and later the COVID-19 pandemic—delayed
its release, which was initially scheduled for July 12, 2019.

21
01:34:51,724 --> 01:34:57,724
During the pandemic, several streaming companies attempted to purchase the streaming rights to the film from Paramount, but all
offers were declined on the orders of Cruise, who insisted that it should be released exclusively in theaters.

22
01:39:22,758 --> 01:39:28,758
Top Gun: Maverick premiered at CinemaCon on April 28, 2022, and was theatrically
released in the United States on May 27 by Paramount Pictures.

23
01:43:53,793 --> 01:43:59,793
The film was widely praised by critics, with many
deeming it superior to its predecessor.

24
01:48:24,827 --> 01:48:30,827
It was named one of the top ten films of 2022 by the National Board of Review and by the American Film Institute and
nominated for six awards at the 95th Academy Awards (including Best Picture), winning Best Sound.

25
01:52:55,862 --> 01:53:01,862
Top Gun: Maverick grossed $1.496 billion worldwide, making it the
second-highest-grossing film of 2022 and the highest-grossing film of Cruise's career.

26
01:57:26,896 --> 01:57:32,896
A sequel is in development.

27
02:01:57,931 --> 02:02:03,931
The film explores themes of fighter pilot, u.s. navy,
sequel, nuclear weapons, military.

28
02:06:28,965 --> 02:06:34,965
The tone is emotional.
